fix(ai): display_image dumped megabytes of base64 in the UI and failed off-terminal

Two symptoms, one root: the display_image tool card stringified its entire
input (base64_data) and output as JSON, and injectIntoActivePty hard-failed
when the active tab was not a terminal.

- tool.tsx: display_image input preview renders "name - KB" instead of the
  raw payload; output renders a one-line confirmation ("displayed in
  terminal (N KB)") or the error; deriveSummary uses the image name.
  Never stringify base64 payloads into the transcript.
- App.tsx: injectIntoActivePty falls back to the most recently active
  terminal tab (tracked via lastTerminalTabIdRef), then to any terminal
  tab, instead of erroring "no active terminal tab to display into".
- compact.ts: new always-on compaction phase elides bulky opaque strings
  (base64-shaped) in tool-call inputs after the call completes - a single
  display_image call was re-sent to the model on every agent step.
  New tests cover elision + non-interference with write_file content.
- sessions.ts: same elision applied to the persisted copy so one image
  call does not blow the 512KB per-session store cap and trim history.

All 254 vitest tests pass; tsc clean. Version 1.5.2
